    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-18T09:39:01+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T09:39:01+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T00:09:01Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T00:09:01Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A large blocking high pressure system persists over the Tasman Sea. An upper level disturbance responsible for precipitation over central and eastern parts will weaken today as a weakening cold front moves across western parts today and across the southeast on Wednesday. A high pressure ridge is expected to develop over South Australia from Wednesday afternoon with weak troughs clipping the southeast in a broad westerly flow on Thursday and Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers south of Leigh Creek, high chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 18 to 30.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:50am to 2:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers east of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning then becoming light in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Yunta. Very high chance of showers about the Gammon Ranges, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h shifting south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 17 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Yunta. Medium chance of showers north of Leigh Creek, most likely in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds southerly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
